HST Office: the wide banner narrows, keeping its ratio, when the tab's groups need the room.

In windows of at least 1280 logical px the banner beside the ribbon was always 360 px wide, so a wide
tab (Insert) shrank and folded its groups beside it. The wide slot now takes the room the current tab's
groups leave at their largest (hst::ribbon::PageFullWidth), from 360 down to 260 logical px, the
narrowest at which the bundled artwork's text stays readable at 1x. The slot keeps the 360:104 ratio,
so the artwork is neither stretched nor cropped, stays centred vertically on the page, and the click
target is the drawn artwork; the page height does not change. A new width replaces the last one only
when it differs by at least 12 logical px, so the banner does not move with small changes of the room.
Windows narrower than 1280 px keep the compact card as before; the impressions are counted as before.

- sfx2 HstBannerGeometry.hxx: MIN_WIDE_ART_WIDTH, WIDE_HYSTERESIS, wideSlotWidth(), slotFor() max width.
- sfx2 HstRibbonBanner.hxx: the last wide slot width; NotebookbarTabControl.cxx: uses it.
- vcl: hst::ribbon::PageFullWidth (include/vcl/HstRibbonWidth.hxx, PriorityMergedHBox.cxx).

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
